From 2ff944f1e3ef38e02f1eb80ce991d6756557aa48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:42:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Memory resources: alignments stricter than the one of the
 memory

The pools of the standard library request blocks aligned on their size
from their upstream resource. The managed memory resources of CUDA and
HIP and the shared space resource of Kokkos refused alignments stricter
than the one of their memory, so a pool over them failed for blocks of
more than 256 bytes. Such alignments are now obtained by over-allocation,
the address of the allocated block being stored before the returned
address (OverAlignedAllocation.hxx).
